From: xenocideend (with Claude Opus 5.5) <xenocideend@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] usb: dwc3: qcom-legacy: don't crash in suspend when the host
 is gone

dwc3_qcom_read_usb2_speed() reads the xHCI host's usb_hcd unconditionally.
If the host failed to probe or restore (xhci probe -110 after a failed
resume) its drvdata is NULL, and the next suspend with wakeup enabled
oopses in dwc3_qcom_suspend().

Return USB_SPEED_UNKNOWN when there is no host, the same answer as when no
device is attached.

Seen on a Retroid Pocket 5 after a failed restore (pstore oops in
dwc3_qcom_suspend). Checked by forcing host mode, unbinding the xhci
driver and suspending: it suspends and resumes cleanly.

---
--- a/drivers/usb/dwc3/dwc3-qcom-legacy.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/dwc3/dwc3-qcom-legacy.c
@@ -326,7 +326,10 @@
 	/*
 	 * FIXME: Fix this layering violation.
 	 */
-	hcd = platform_get_drvdata(dwc->xhci);
+	hcd = dwc->xhci ? platform_get_drvdata(dwc->xhci) : NULL;
+	/* no host (xhci failed to probe or restore): nothing to read, and no crash */
+	if (!hcd || !hcd->self.root_hub)
+		return USB_SPEED_UNKNOWN;
 
 #ifdef CONFIG_USB
 	udev = usb_hub_find_child(hcd->self.root_hub, port_index + 1);
